# Keep the build context small + deterministic — anything listed here is
# never COPY'd into the image, even if the Dockerfile says `COPY . .`.
# Rule of thumb: if it's in .gitignore, it almost certainly belongs here.

# Dependencies (re-installed via npm ci inside the image)
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output (regenerated inside the image)
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
out
**/out
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite
**/.vite
.turbo
.cache
.parcel-cache

# Client bundle — client ships to Vercel, not Railway. Excluding its
# source here would break the monorepo npm ci, so we keep client/src
# but drop its build artefacts above.

# Environment + secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
google-service-account.json
server/gmail-token.json
gmail-token.json
**/service-account*.json
**/*-credentials.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12

# DB files
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
server/jobs.db*
server/data
server/resumes

# Git metadata
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Editor / IDE
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*~
.claude

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Logs
*.log
logs

# External / vendored repos — never ship these
career-ops-main
humanizer-main
ULTIMATE_JOB_SCRAPER
Resume_rewrite_feature
UI_RESOURCE

# Local scratch
JOURNAL.md
LINKEDIN_URL_GUIDE.md
MIGRATION_STATUS.md
dublinjobintelligence.md
test-*.pdf
test-*.json

# Alternate deploy configs — Dockerfile is the source of truth now
nixpacks.toml
railpack.json
